# ARC Language Module v0.24

A governed, auditable multilingual language/script/lineage substrate.
Separates graph truth from runtime capability, and package-owned data from external corpus dependencies.

---

## What this package actually is

- A **SQLite-backed language graph** covering 34 seeded languages, 14 families, scripts, aliases, lineage edges, and phonology/transliteration profiles.
- A **governed ingestion pipeline** for Glottolog-style, ISO 639-3-style, and CLDR-style corpora — with dry-run mode, conflict detection, dedup reporting, and provenance tracking.
- A **runtime routing layer** that separates knowing a language exists from being able to translate or speak it.
- An **operator tooling layer**: acquisition workspace, coverage reports, implementation matrix, evidence bundles, conflict review exports.
- An **honest gap-tracking system**: every missing corpus is declared in manifests; every unsupported runtime is marked explicitly; no fake support.

---

## What this package is not

- A full translation engine (local seeded phrase translation only; Argos/NLLB are optional external dependencies)
- A full TTS/speech system (PersonaPlex and similar are boundary stubs only)
- A complete phonemic inventory (phonology profiles are broad IPA hints, not full phoneme sets)
- A character-level transliteration engine (profiles declare schemes; mapping tables are not bundled)

---

## Quick start

```bash
pip install -e .

python -m arc_lang.cli.main init-db
python -m arc_lang.cli.main seed-common-languages
python -m arc_lang.cli.main stats
python -m arc_lang.cli.main detect "hola gracias"
python -m arc_lang.cli.main lineage lang:spa
python -m arc_lang.cli.main coverage-report
python -m arc_lang.cli.main system-status
```

---

## Core capabilities (package-owned, complete)

| Surface | CLI | API |
|---------|-----|-----|
| Language graph (34 languages, 14 families) | `stats`, `search-languages`, `lineage` | `GET /stats`, `GET /lineage/{id}` |
| Script detection + transliteration | `detect-script`, `transliterate` | `GET /detect`, `GET /transliterate` |
| Language aliases (endonym/exonym/romanized) | `upsert-language-alias`, `list-language-aliases` | `POST /aliases/upsert` |
| Language variants (dialect/register/orthography) | `upsert-language-variant` | `POST /languages/variants/upsert` |
| Custom lineage assertions + arbitration | `add-custom-lineage`, `effective-lineage` | `POST /lineage/custom` |
| Language submission + governance review | `submit-language-inline`, `review-target` | `POST /languages/submit` |
| Phonology profiles (12 languages seeded) | `upsert-phonology-profile`, `phonology-hint` | `POST /phonology/profiles/upsert` |
| Transliteration profiles (11 entries seeded) | `upsert-transliteration-profile` | `POST /transliterate` |
| Semantic concept graph | `upsert-semantic-concept`, `link-concept` | `POST /concepts/upsert` |
| Provider registry + health | `register-provider`, `set-provider-health` | `POST /providers/register` |
| Runtime routing (translation + speech) | `runtime-translate`, `runtime-speak` | `POST /runtime/translate` |
| Runtime receipts | `list-runtime-receipts` | `GET /runtime/receipts` |
| Provider action catalogs + execution | `provider-action-catalog`, `execute-provider-action` | `POST /providers/actions/execute` |
| Translation install plans | `translation-install-plan` | `GET /runtime/install-plan/translation` |
| Operator policy | `show-policy`, `set-policy` | `GET /policy` |
| System status | `system-status` | `GET /system-status` |
| Evidence export | `export-evidence` | `POST /evidence/export` |
| Conflict review export | `export-conflict-review` | `POST /conflicts/export` |
| Coverage report | `coverage-report` | `POST /coverage/report` |
| Implementation matrix | `build-implementation-matrix` | `POST /implementation-matrix` |
| Acquisition workspace | `plan-acquisition-job`, `validate-staged-asset`, `export-ingestion-workspace` | `POST /acquisition/jobs` |
| Batch import/export | `batch-import`, `batch-export` | `POST /batch/import` |
| Source authority weights | `set-source-weight`, `list-source-weights` | `POST /sources/weights/set` |

---

## Ingestion

```bash
# Dry-run first (no writes, shows conflicts and record counts)
python -m arc_lang.cli.main import-glottolog-fixture path/to/glottolog.csv --dry-run

# Live import
python -m arc_lang.cli.main import-glottolog-fixture path/to/glottolog.csv
python -m arc_lang.cli.main import-iso-fixture path/to/iso639-3.csv
python -m arc_lang.cli.main import-cldr-fixture path/to/cldr.json
```

All imports: idempotent, provenance-tracked, dedup-reported (inserted vs updated), conflict-aware.

---

## Coverage reporting

```bash
python -m arc_lang.cli.main coverage-report
python -m arc_lang.cli.main coverage-report --language-id lang:jpn --language-id lang:kor
python -m arc_lang.cli.main coverage-report --output-path coverage.json
```

Coverage reports include per-language: alias count by type, script count, phonology profiles,
transliteration profiles, lineage edge count, capability summary, and 4 honest gap flags
(`missing_phonology`, `missing_transliteration`, `missing_pronunciation`, `missing_script`).

---

## Phonology

12 languages have seeded broad IPA phonology profiles: English, Spanish, French, German,
Russian, Hindi, Japanese, Korean, Mandarin Chinese, Arabic (MSA), Turkish, Thai.

```bash
python -m arc_lang.cli.main phonology-hint "こんにちは" lang:jpn
python -m arc_lang.cli.main list-phonology-profiles --language-id lang:rus
```

These are **hints only** — not full phonemic inventories. See `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_MANIFESTS_AND_PHONOLOGY.md`.

---

## Acquisition workspace

```bash
python -m arc_lang.cli.main plan-acquisition-job Glottolog --stage-name staging
python -m arc_lang.cli.main record-staged-asset <job_id> /path/to/file.csv --asset-kind csv
python -m arc_lang.cli.main validate-staged-asset /path/to/file.csv csv
python -m arc_lang.cli.main list-acquisition-jobs
python -m arc_lang.cli.main export-ingestion-workspace workspace.json
```

---

## External dependencies (not installed by default)

| Provider | What it enables | How to enable |
|----------|----------------|---------------|
| `argostranslate` | Local neural machine translation | `pip install argostranslate` + model download |
| NLLB | Large-scale neural MT | External model server (bridge stub only) |
| PersonaPlex | Neural speech synthesis | NVIDIA API (boundary stub only) |

The package will run fully without any of these. External providers are declared in backend manifests
and tracked in the implementation matrix. Runtime routing will report `unavailable` for unsupported
pairs rather than silently failing.

---

## Running tests

```bash
python -m pytest tests/ -q
# 99 tests, all pass
```

---

## Architecture

See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the full separation of concerns:
language vs script, lineage vs identifier, translation equivalence vs etymological relatedness,
pronunciation hint vs phonology truth, graph truth vs runtime capability.
